BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Traditional Irish Music Irish Music Diarmuid Ó Meachair-accordion
  & melodeon\, Ellie Egan-fiddle\, John Hannigan-accordion\, Simon Lace-gui
 tar
DTSTART:20260928T160000
DTEND:20260928T170000
DTSTAMP:20260913T151921Z
UID:c206df0535b0fbe888dbe776693e68@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Accordion player Diarmuid Ó Meachair and Galway fiddle player
  Ellie Egan will play a selection of music from East Galway. The tradition
 al music of East Galway is known for its unhurried pace\, lyrical expressi
 on\, and strong rhythm. Unlike the faster\, highly ornamented styles of ot
 her regions like Sligo\, the East Galway style focuses closely on the smoo
 th flow of the melody and a soulful\, down-to-earth feel. The concert will
  include music from legendary east Galway figures such as Paddy Fahey\, Pa
 ddy Kelly\, Conor Tully\, Paddy Carty and Joe Burke. They will be accompan
 ied by guitarist Simon Lace and Brooks Scholar John Hannigan (Accordion & 
 Fiddle). Dress Code: Casual (jeans ok) --- Event Details: https://myhc.hol
 ycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152725 Source: College of the Holy Cross Event page: h
 ttps://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152725\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 mil
 es of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from worcester-co
 lleges-events.ics\nSource page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152725
LOCATION:Brooks Concert Hall\, 1 College Street\, Worcester\, MA 01610\, U
 nited States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152725
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vibe Check: Body Language and Signals
DTSTART:20260928T230000
DTEND:20260929T000000
DTSTAMP:20260913T151921Z
UID:d386ce5b8bd1ddc6ac4cca76029522@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to read between the lines! Join us for an interactiv
 e workshop exploring body language\, nonverbal signals\, and consent. Lear
 n how signals can be misunderstood\, practice ways to clearly ask for cons
 ent\, and get familiar with the CROSS acronym. Through fun group challenge
 s and discussion\, we’ll explore why clear communication matters and why
  we shouldn’t rely on assumptions when it comes to consent. --- Event De
 tails: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154155 Source: College of the H
 oly Cross Event page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154155\n\nEvents
